@base = http://localhost:3000

### Health
GET {{base}}/health

### Create incident
# TEMPORARY (Week 1): created_by is sent in the body because there is no auth yet.
# It is not a trusted identity. Week 2 reads the user from the JWT.
POST {{base}}/api/incidents
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Suspicious DNS tunnelling", "description": "High volume TXT queries", "severity": "high", "created_by": 2, "assigned_to": 3 }

### List (filters + pagination)
GET {{base}}/api/incidents?status=investigating&severity=high&page=1&limit=10

### Get one
GET {{base}}/api/incidents/1

### Update fields (status is NOT allowed here)
PATCH {{base}}/api/incidents/2
Content-Type: application/json

{ "assigned_to": 2, "severity": "high" }

### Add a note only
POST {{base}}/api/incidents/2/updates
Content-Type: application/json

{ "author_id": 2, "note": "Reached out to the finance user for the original email." }

### Change status (records previous_status -> new_status, one transaction)
POST {{base}}/api/incidents/2/updates
Content-Type: application/json

{ "author_id": 2, "note": "Link detonated in sandbox, credential harvester confirmed.", "new_status": "investigating" }

### History, oldest first
GET {{base}}/api/incidents/2/updates

### Delete (its updates are deleted with it)
DELETE {{base}}/api/incidents/4

### ERROR: validation (400)
POST {{base}}/api/incidents
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "x", "severity": "nope" }

### ERROR: status via PATCH (400 STATUS_VIA_UPDATES)
PATCH {{base}}/api/incidents/2
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "closed" }

### ERROR: not allowed transition, open -> resolved (409)
POST {{base}}/api/incidents/2/updates
Content-Type: application/json

{ "author_id": 2, "note": "Skipping ahead", "new_status": "resolved" }

### ERROR: unknown incident (404)
GET {{base}}/api/incidents/999
